  m_Name: 1988 jaywalking
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Jaywalking Offense 1988
  info: Jaywalking, or crossing roads outside designated pedestrian crossings, is
    strictly prohibited to ensure pedestrian and traffic safety. The government enforces
    this law to reduce accidents caused by pedestrians crossing in unsafe areas.
    Violators are subject to fines of SGD 20 for first offenses and up to SGD 1,000
    for repeat violations or dangerous crossings. Public education campaigns encourage
    pedestrians to use overhead bridges, zebra crossings, and traffic lights for
    safe road usage.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1c6bae48f1a1947199cc01971b7bbcc3, type: 3}
